Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:56:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] NOT-FOR-UPSTREAM: soundwire: qcom: switch banks on both multi-master
 controllers

On a multi-master link (Glymur: swr2 primary, swr1 dependent providing
two extra lanes) the SCP_FrameCtrl broadcast that ends a bank switch is
fanned out as unicast writes to each peripheral, on the primary only,
because the primary's broadcast never reported SPECIAL_CMD_ID_FINISHED.
The peripherals switch banks that way, but neither controller does:
MCP_STATUS reads bank 0 on both swr1 and swr2 at all times, while the
bus bookkeeping alternates between banks. The DPn registers the core
writes for "the next bank" are then the dependent's live registers, so
a port enable on swr1 takes effect at the moment of the register write,
not at the bank switch, and the port starts at an arbitrary point
relative to the codec's.

On the ASUS Zenbook A16 the WCD9378 headphone port (codec DP6) is fed by
swr1 DP1. Its left/right orientation was random per stream start: 60 of
120 starts came out swapped (440 Hz on the left channel captured on the
right, checked on a line-in loopback), and clearing and restoring swr1
DP1's channel enables mid-stream re-drew the orientation, while doing the
same to the codec's DP6 did not.

The broadcast has to go out through both controllers' command FIFOs:
queued on the dependent first, the primary's broadcast then completes
and both controllers switch banks together with the peripherals. Do
that for SCP_FrameCtrl writes on a primary with a dependent, instead of
the unicast fan-out, and warn when the two controllers are found in
different banks before a switch.

The dependent does not need to be waited for: its command FIFO reads
empty right after the write, before the primary's broadcast is queued.

Tested on the A16: every bank switch finished, both controllers'
MCP_STATUS bank bits toggled with each switch, and the headphone
orientation was correct in 100 of 100 starts after boot (on each of
two boots) and 10 of 10 on each of three more. Across system sleep the
dependent needs the following patch as well.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5)
